# Finished disease-panel generations stay on the machine that made them and
# out of git entirely. This repository's only remote is the public destination,
# so a tracked run output is one `git push` away from being published
# permanently. Ignoring the whole directory makes that impossible rather than
# merely discouraged; the files themselves are untouched on disk.
disease_runs/

# The periodically updated "Global List of Medical Screening Tools" and the
# fact-check notes beside it are a local working reference, not part of the
# package. Kept out of the public repository until the user asks otherwise.
/Global List of Medical Computational Screening Tools folder/

# The working agreement for this checkout stays local. It names destinations,
