# --- Screening tools: third-party code relocated from DATA_PATH -------------
# Third-party screening code now lives in "screening subpackage/<tool>/" so the
# tooling sits beside the repository instead of in the data volume. Weights,
# example inputs, reference tables and databases deliberately stay under
# DATA_PATH and never appear here.
#
# The payload itself is NOT tracked, for three concrete reasons:
#   * the five installed virtual environments are ~5.2 GB and each has 10-35
#     files hard-coding this machine's absolute paths, including a home
#     directory (/home/<name>/...), which must never reach a public repository;
#   * CrossAbSense and ThermoMPNN are upstream clones carrying their own .git,
#     which git would otherwise record as bare gitlinks pointing nowhere;
#   * all of it is reproducible from the installers, which ARE tracked.
#
# Ignore broadly and re-include the small files on purpose: a missed negation
# costs one untracked file, while a missed ignore costs gigabytes in a public
# repository. Verify after any edit with:
#   git check-ignore -v "screening subpackage/<tool>/venv/bin/python"
screening subpackage/**
# Let git descend so the negations below can match.
!screening subpackage/**/
# Tracked on purpose: the recipe, never the payload.
!screening subpackage/README.md
!screening subpackage/NOTICE
!screening subpackage/.gitignore
!screening subpackage/*/manifest.toml
!screening subpackage/*/LICENSE
!screening subpackage/*/LICENCE
!screening subpackage/*/NOTICE
!screening subpackage/*/install_*.py
!screening subpackage/*/README.md
# Re-exclude the payload even where a negation above might otherwise catch it.
screening subpackage/*/venv/
screening subpackage/*/CrossAbSense/
screening subpackage/*/ThermoMPNN/
